# Load testing on {{ inventory_hostname }}

Managed by the `loadtest` role in pulibrary/princeton_ansible.

| Tool   | Version                       | Command          |
|--------|-------------------------------|------------------|
| JMeter | {{ loadtest_jmeter_version }} | `jmeter`         |
| k6     | {{ loadtest_k6_version }}     | `k6`             |

Put test plans in `jmeter/`, k6 scripts in `k6/`, and output in `results/`.

## JMeter (always run non-GUI on this server)

    jmeter -n -t jmeter/plan.jmx -l results/plan.jtl -e -o results/plan-report

## k6

    k6 run -e TARGET=https://example.princeton.edu k6/smoke.js

Load tests generate real traffic. Coordinate with the owners of the target
service before pointing anything at production.
